---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How many machines a pile of messages needs, how big a time bucket can be, and how much of a read spike one coalesced read absorbs. The sliders hold round numbers for practice, not Discord's data.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Messages stored (billions) <input type="range" min="100" max="5000" step="100" value="1000" data-m /> <b data-mval></b></label>
      <label>Stored size per message (bytes) <input type="range" min="100" max="1000" step="50" value="300" data-b /> <b data-bval></b></label>
      <label>Copies of each message (replication factor) <input type="range" min="1" max="5" value="3" data-r /> <b data-rval></b></label>
      <label>Disk kept in use (%) <input type="range" min="30" max="90" step="5" value="75" data-f /> <b data-fval></b></label>
      <label>Messages per day in the busiest channel (thousands) <input type="range" min="5" max="500" step="5" value="100" data-p /> <b data-pval></b></label>
      <label>Bucket length (days) <input type="range" min="1" max="30" value="10" data-d /> <b data-dval></b></label>
      <label>Readers of one hot row per second <input type="range" min="500" max="20000" step="500" value="5000" data-q /> <b data-qval></b></label>
      <label>Time for one database read (ms) <input type="range" min="5" max="100" step="5" value="20" data-t /> <b data-tval></b></label>
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: one trillion is 1,000 billion, and a terabyte is a million megabytes. The 4 TB and 9 TB per node are the averages Discord reported in 2023 for its Cassandra and ScyllaDB nodes; whether a node's disk is that full, and how large a stored message is, are guesses here, and the sliders let you change them. The 100 MB partition limit is the figure from Discord's 2017 post. For the hot row, a data service instance routes by channel, so one instance gets every request, and it runs one database read for the row at a time, starting the next when the last ends; everyone who arrives meanwhile joins that read.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const val = (s: string) => Number(q<HTMLInputElement>(s).value);
    const OUT_ROWS = 9; // lines in the result list
    const CASSANDRA_TB = 4, SCYLLA_TB = 9; // average disk per node reported by Discord in 2023
    const LIMIT_MB = 100; // partition size Discord wanted to stay under
    const BILLION = 1e9, TB = 1e12, MB = 1e6, MS_PER_S = 1000;
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const fmt = (n: number) => (n >= 100 ? Math.round(n) : Math.round(n * 10) / 10).toLocaleString('en-US');
    function draw() {
      const msgs = val('[data-m]') * BILLION; const size = val('[data-b]'); const copies = val('[data-r]'); const fill = val('[data-f]') / 100;
      const perDay = val('[data-p]') * 1000; const days = val('[data-d]'); const readers = val('[data-q]'); const readMs = val('[data-t]');
      ['m', 'b', 'r', 'f', 'p', 'd', 'q', 't'].forEach((k) => (q(`[data-${k}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${k}]`))));
      const rawTb = (msgs * size) / TB;
      const stored = rawTb * copies;
      const partitionMb = (perDay * days * size) / MB;
      const fitDays = Math.floor((LIMIT_MB * MB) / (perDay * size));
      const coalesced = Math.min(readers, MS_PER_S / readMs);
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Data before copies (TB)', fmt(rawTb)],
        ['Data on disk with all copies (TB)', fmt(stored)],
        [`Nodes needed at ${CASSANDRA_TB} TB per node`, fmt(Math.ceil(stored / (CASSANDRA_TB * fill)))],
        [`Nodes needed at ${SCYLLA_TB} TB per node`, fmt(Math.ceil(stored / (SCYLLA_TB * fill)))],
        ['Busiest channel: partition size per bucket (MB)', fmt(partitionMb)],
        [`Longest bucket that stays under ${LIMIT_MB} MB (days)`, fitDays >= 1 ? fmt(fitDays) : 'under 1'],
        ['Database reads per second for the hot row, no coalescing', fmt(readers)],
        ['Database reads per second for the hot row, coalesced', fmt(coalesced)],
        ['Requests that join a read already running (%)', `${fmt(100 * (1 - coalesced / readers))}%`],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
